Acceptance criteria:
  Every actual workstream retains the eight required fields and a stable ID.
  Issues and Project items track actual workstreams, not this index or ledger.

Completion evidence:
  ic-01 foundation is complete locally; Project 13 tracks six issue-backed items.
  Verified read-back: #1 CLOSED/COMPLETED/Done; #2/#3/#4/#5 OPEN/In Progress;
  #6 OPEN/Todo. Fresh conflict check and independent complete-body
  verification preserve all six original issue/item mappings and backlinks.
  ic-02 records the voice/wake/Agency/3D-mesh requirements and prototype exception.
  ic-04/ic-05 qualification informs remaining ic-02 decisions before ic-06.
  ic-06 has an authorized, locally verified early Electron fixture UI;
  it does not waive live prerequisites or authorize continuous audio/agent access.
  A later request authorizes microphone selection/brief device checks and an
  unsigned Windows portable prerelease. v0.1.0-prototype.1 is published, nondraft;
  its source tag and independently downloaded EXE/checksum are verified.
  The separately requested branding is implemented and verified in a local,
  unpublished v0.1.0-prototype.2 candidate; .1 remains unchanged. Native/EXE/UI
  icons use the refined microphone-and-mesh artwork. ic-06 remains IN_PROGRESS.
  Deep research records technology alternatives, runtime contracts and
  performance evidence in docs; recommendation is not selection/qualification.
  ic-04/ic-05 now progress under explicit bounded conversation/speech authority:
  installed local-English push-to-talk, exact existing idle session, no work
  tools, cloud audio or new sessions. The packaged real capture/transcription/
  existing-session response/local-playback loop and actual portable launcher
  pass in .3. Evidence is recorded in ic-06; broader criteria, speed qualification
  and hardware/human acceptance are not complete.
  Current .4 candidate adds actual published-mesh startup, confirmed ACP work,
  one atomic receipt and observed activity. The exact approved native read-only
  tool/response/speech test passes; saved grants meant zero native prompts.
  Twelve packaged desktop cases and actual portable real-mesh startup pass.
  .4 is unsigned/unpublished; manual terminal entry, human/performance and
  native permission-prompt qualification remain explicit open gates.

  The separate .5 candidate adds close graph zoom/pan/reset and native window
  maximize/restore, preserving normal bounds and prior maximization through
  floating mode. All 14 packaged desktop cases and actual portable startup pass.
  .4 is preserved; .5 remains unsigned/local/unpublished with no new live task.

  The separate .6 candidate makes floating movement/size controls always
  discoverable with Drag to move and Smaller/Larger/native size readout.
  All 15 packaged desktop cases and actual portable real-mesh startup pass;
  sizing preserves graph zoom/workspace bounds and respects monitor limits.
  .4/.5 remain preserved; .6 is unsigned/local/unpublished.

  The separate .7 candidate adds installed-voice profiles and pitch/rate/volume,
  draft preview and atomic persistence, with a cancellable provider boundary.
  Richer arbitrary identity/timbre/emotion remain mandatory future requirements.
  All 17 packaged cases and actual portable startup/profile persistence pass.
  Prior builds remain preserved. The unsigned .7 prerelease is now published
  from source 3147d492574980f6c89cc8e9a32920efb859f253; independent anonymous
  downloads match the qualified EXE/checksum. Broader acceptance stays open.

  The README presentation milestone adds a 432 px animated hero and captioned
  image navigation/gallery; docs/guide.md preserves the former entry text.
  Existing #5 mirrors the milestone after all six body baselines matched;
  independent complete-body read-back verifies unchanged mappings/states/stages.
  No runtime/release asset changed and ic-06 remains IN_PROGRESS.

  ic-06 additionally implements on-demand node names and pinned details in
  local source, with keyboard access and no dispatch retargeting. Six focused
  desktop cases cover picking, dragging, floating fit, navigation and idle/
  minimized scheduling; broader product criteria and .7 release stay unchanged.
  Only existing #5 was mirrored after all six prior body hashes matched;
  fresh complete-body read-back verifies unchanged mappings/states/stages.

  ic-06 microphone fix removes the session gate from local capture/transcription.
  Disconnected transcripts remain editable and unsent; connection alone never
  dispatches. A separate unsigned .8 candidate and actual portable recording/
  cancellation pass using synthetic input. Published .7 and user app untouched.
  Broader physical-device/human/performance criteria remain open.

  ic-06 recognition-review fix retains low-confidence and over-limit text,
  requires explicit review/shortening and prevents automatic dispatch/work
  preparation in every destination. Separate unsigned .9 candidate passes
  native, focused packaged and actual portable checks; .7/.8 remain unchanged.
  Recognition accuracy and physical FDUCE/human acceptance remain unqualified.

  ic-06 floating microphone replaces the inert live footer with one operational
  control outside the default-collapsed dock. View changes retain capture;
  one-row dock and visible floating review/errors/settings are packaged in the
  separate unsigned .10 candidate. Seventeen focused packaged cases and actual
  portable synthetic capture/cancel pass. Published .7 and user app untouched.

